,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected.\r\n\r\n**Testing project:** [test_pr_102286.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18741061/test_pr_102286.zip)\r\n\r\nNote that it won't work if the CSGBox you're moving is a child of the CSGCombiner3D with the collision on it. It will just pass through instead:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/41a9cfbe-4601-414d-ac92-d7b87e30df0c\r\n\r\nThis may be difficult to resolve though, given the collision shape is regenerating itself in real-time when you're moving the object (and you don't want the object to collide with itself as you're repositioning it).\r\n\r\nPS: I noticed that we can pan, zoom and orbit while using physics-based repositioning, but not when using the translate/rotate/style Blender-style manipulation shortcuts. It would be good to look into unlocking those options if they don't conflict with anything else (in a separate PR).\r\n","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102286#pullrequestreview-2607210457","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102286","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102286#pullrequestreview-2607210457"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102286"}},"submitted_at":"2025-02-10T21:27:21Z","commit_id":null},{"id":2607214437,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6bZu9l","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","ava